From e6dcec062781ace7c379134a704cdf811440c2c8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Caires <DanielMarques.Caires@windriver.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Feb 2026 14:28:23 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] Create orphan instances sanitizer in Nova

Add an init container (nova-orphan-instances-sanitizer) to the
nova-compute daemonset that cleans up libvirt domains not owned
by Nova before the compute service starts.

Also add a CronJob (nova-instances-sanitizer) for periodic
orphan cleanup on a configurable schedule.

Changes to the Nova chart:
- Add _orphan-instances-sanitizer.sh.tpl script template
- Add orphan-instances-sanitizer.sh entry to configmap-bin
  (gated by init_container_instances_sanitizer OR
  cron_job_instances_sanitizer)
- Add cron-job-instances-sanitizer.yaml template
- Add init container to daemonset-compute.yaml (guarded by
  manifests.init_container_instances_sanitizer)
- Add nova_sanitizer image, job config, dependencies,
  security contexts, and resource definitions to values.yaml
- Add manifests flags (both disabled by default):
  cron_job_instances_sanitizer and
  init_container_instances_sanitizer

Notes on intentional deviations from CronJob conventions:
- nodeSelector uses agent.compute labels instead of job labels
  because the sanitizer requires host-level access to the
  libvirt socket at /run/libvirt/libvirt-sock, which only
  exists on compute nodes.
- pod.resources.sanitizer is a top-level resource key (not
  under pod.resources.jobs) because it is shared between the
  CronJob container and the init container in
  daemonset-compute.yaml.

Change-Id: I13b33c9eae6385d785ba005617536a88e7b2f59c
Signed-off-by: Daniel Caires <DanielMarques.Caires@windriver.com>
